      "description": "Delta State University Applicant Portal | Part-Time Certified Police Officer Skip to Main Content About Academics admissions Student Life Athletics Alumni & Friends my DSU Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Part-Time Certified Police Officer Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. You must attach proof of certification as a Law Enforcement Officer from a POST agency in MS or another State, and be eligible for transfer if outside MS. Posting Details Position Information Job Title Part-Time Certified Police Officer Working Title Reserve Police Officer PT Position Type Staff Department Police Department and Campus Safety Posting Number 201201440 Full or Part Time Part Time Benefit Eligible No If Other, Please Explain: Tenure/Non-Tenure Track Non-Tenure Track Salary Basis Hourly If Other, Please Explain: Position Summary Information Responsibilities The officer is responsible for protecting life and property utilizing effective crime prevention techniques, and apprehending criminals. The officer will enforce university, state, and applicable federal laws, regulations, and policies. The officer may be assigned to traffic and crowd control as well as securing buildings after business operations have ceased. The officer must be able to act soundly without direct supervision and to exercise independent judgment in dealing with emergency situations. Qualifications Must be physically fit and be able to walk, run, climb, and crawl to the extent prescribed by the Board on Law Enforcement Standards and Training. Candidate must have good verbal communication as well as written communication skills. Must be able to operate a motor vehicle including a car, truck, golf cart, ATV , bicycle, or other all-terrain vehicles. The candidate must be a board-certified police officer. Salary Commensurate with experience and qualifications Minimum Qualifications High School Diploma or GED . Applicants must be certified as a Law Enforcement Officer through P.O.S.T. (Peace Officers Standard and Training) or currently in the Academy. Must have a valid Mississippi Drivers License. Preferred Qualifications Prior Campus Law Enforcement Experience Sixty hours of College coursework, an Associate’s Degree or an undergraduate degree in a related field is preferred. Special Instructions to Applicants You must attach proof of certification as a Law Enforcement Officer from a POST agency in MS or another State, and be eligible for transfer if outside MS. Additional Information Start Date of Employment to be Determined Posting Detail Information Open Date 10/05/2023 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? DSU Employee DSU Job Website Invited by Department to Apply MS State Employment Service HigherEdJobs Chronicle of Higher Education Diverse Issues Indeed.com Other * Do you have a high school degree or a GED? Yes No What type of driver's license do you have? Do not have a Driver's License A regular Operator's License A Commercial Driver's License * Are you currently certified as a law enforcement officer in Mississippi by the State (BLEOST) or in another state and able to transfer certification within one year? yes no other state * Do you have any experience in campus law enforcement? Yes No * Will you now or in the future require \"sponsorship\" for an employment based visa status? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Re