    "https://deltastate.peopleadmin.com/postings/5073": {
      "title": "McNair Scholars Program Director",
      "description": "Delta State University Applicant Portal | McNair Scholars Program Director Skip to Main Content About Academics admissions Student Life Athletics Alumni & Friends my DSU Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help McNair Scholars Program Director Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title McNair Scholars Program Director Working Title McNair Scholars Program Director Position Type Staff Department Grants and Contracts Posting Number 201201698 Full or Part Time Full Time Benefit Eligible Yes If Other, Please Explain: Tenure/Non-Tenure Track Salary Basis 12 month If Other, Please Explain: Position Summary Information Responsibilities The Program Director will be responsible for the day-to-day operations of the McNair Scholars Program. The Program Director will report to the Executive Director of Sponsored Programs and Special Projects in the Office of Institutional Grants. The Program Director will have the authority and responsibility to monitor all activities and ensure that university and federal regulations, guidelines, policies, and procedures are followed. The ideal candidate will have knowledge of the target area and its educational and economic challenges and assets. This position will be responsible for the tasks outlined in the Plan of Operation (available upon request). Qualifications Master’s degree required, Master’s in a STEM field preferred Three years of experience in higher education administration, advising, management or counseling Strong knowledge of academic research, ideally with at least one published academic article and experience supervising student research Experience managing or implementing federal grant funding Excellent verbal and written communication skills and time management skills Experience directly advising and mentoring students similar to McNair Research Scholars Committed to the mission and vision of the McNair Program Strong preference to a candidate who is a McNair alumnus Strong preference to a candidate with professional experience in a STEM field Strong preference to a candidate with experience working in a TRIO program Salary Commensurate with experience, qualifications, and university’s resources. Minimum Qualifications Preferred Qualifications Special Instructions to Applicants Additional Information Posting Detail Information Open Date 04/07/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? DSU Employee DSU Job Website Invited by Department to Apply MS State Employment Service HigherEdJobs Chronicle of Higher Education Diverse Issues Indeed.com Other * Will you now or in the future require \"sponsorship\" for an employment based visa status? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Unofficial Transcripts Letter of Reference 1 Letter of Reference 2 Optional Documents Other Document Letter of Reference 3 Delta State University is an Equal Employment Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer. Delta State University is committed to maintaining a learning and working environment free from sexual and gender-based discrimination or harassment. Our goal is for all to have equal access to the many great services and opportunities we offer. For more information, or to report an incident, see https://www.deltastate.edu/titleix/ or email titleix@deltastate.edu . To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
