    "https://deltastate.peopleadmin.com/postings/4736": {
      "title": "Housekeeper (Two Positions Available)",
      "description": "Delta State University Applicant Portal | Housekeeper (Two Positions Available) Skip to Main Content About Academics admissions Student Life Athletics Alumni & Friends my DSU Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Housekeeper (Two Positions Available) Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Housekeeper (Two Positions Available) Working Title Housekeeper (Two Positions Available) Position Type Staff Department Housekeeping Posting Number 201201476 Full or Part Time Full Time Benefit Eligible Yes If Other, Please Explain: Tenure/Non-Tenure Track Non-Tenure Track Salary Basis Hourly If Other, Please Explain: Position Summary Information Responsibilities Perform routine and more complex custodial duties. Cleans and dusts areas such as suites, offices, classrooms, kitchens, living spaces, laboratories, lobbies, museums, locker rooms, stairways, corridors and elevators. Dust mop and wet mop floors. Cleans and polishes furniture and cleans windows. Spray buffs, strips, seals and waxes floors as instructed using appropriate equipment. Cleans and maintains restrooms and bathrooms. Clean glass, chalkboards, display cases, interior partitions, light fixtures, etc. Refills toilet paper, paper towel, and soap dispensers. Cleans and polishes hardware such as door handles, push plates, kick plates, metal handrails, drinking fountains, and restroom trim (external piping, faucets, traps and valves). Vacuum, spot clean and shampoos carpets. Removes and cleans floor mats and entrance rug runners. Wash walls, doors and woodwork. Moves furniture and equipment as required. Maintain storage areas in a clean and orderly manner. Maintain adequate supply of cleaning equipment, materials and supplies. Use cleaning tools such as mops, brooms, squeegees, cleaning cloths, sponges, pails brushes, vacuum cleaners and floor machines. Turn in found articles in accordance with University policy. Removes trash and trash containers from buildings to designated disposal areas. Reports all repairs required and safety and fire hazards to building secretary and immediate supervisor. Observe safety standards and practices. Perform related duties as required or assigned within job classification. Lift and carry objects of at least 30-60 pounds unassisted, assist others in moving objects greater than 30-60 pounds. Clean exterior windows on upper level buildings using commercial man lifts or other specified equipment. Assist in employee training when necessary. Must be available to work extra hours and weekends. Qualifications Minimum of two years in cleaning services or related type work. Ability to read, write and follow written instructions. A valid MS driver’s license required. Salary Commensurate with experience, qualifications, and university’s resources. Minimum Qualifications Minimum of one year in cleaning services or related type work. Ability to read, write and follow written instructions. Must have a valid drivers license. Preferred Qualifications Minimum of two years in cleaning services or related type work. Ability to read, write and follow written instructions. A valid MS driver’s license required. Special Instructions to Applicants Additional Information Posting Detail Information Open Date 04/03/2024 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? DSU Employee DSU Job Website Invited by Department to Apply MS State Employment Service HigherEdJobs Chronicle of Higher Education Diverse Issues Indeed.com Other * Do you have a valid, current driver's license? yes no Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Delta State University is an Equal Employment Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer. Delta State University is committed to maintaining a learning and working environment free from sexual and gender-based discrimination or harassment. Our goal is for all to have equal access to the many great services and opportunities we offer. For more information, or to report an incident, see https://www.deltastate.edu/titleix/ or email titleix@deltastate.edu . To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
