    "https://deltastate.peopleadmin.com/postings/5113": {
      "title": "Assistant Athletic Trainer",
      "description": "Delta State University Applicant Portal | Assistant Athletic Trainer Skip to Main Content About Academics admissions Student Life Athletics Alumni & Friends my DSU Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Athletic Trainer Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Requires a high periods of concentration intermittently and normal attention. Lifting of equipment and injured student-athletes is required. Will require work outside in hot environments. Posting Details Position Information Job Title Assistant Athletic Trainer Working Title Assistant Athletic Trainer Position Type Staff Department Trainer Posting Number 201201699 Full or Part Time Full Time Benefit Eligible Yes If Other, Please Explain: Tenure/Non-Tenure Track Non-Tenure Track Salary Basis 12 month If Other, Please Explain: Position Summary Information Responsibilities Assist in the care, treatment, prevention and rehabilitation of injured student-athletes. Work with team physicians/office staff to coordinate referrals, office visits and surgeries. Furthermore, the assistant will provide direct athletic training coverage for assigned intercollegiate athletics teams as determined by supervisor. Coverage will involve practice and games, will include nights, weekends and travel. Supervise graduate assistants. Administrative duties will include coordinating the secondary insurance program for student-athlete medical expenses. Will be required to abide by all Delta State University, Gulf South Conference and NCAA rules and regulations. Additional duties as assigned by supervisor. Qualifications Masters Degree Required. NATABOC Certification Required. Eligible for State of Mississippi Athletic Training Licensure/current holder of license. CPR /First Aid/ AED certification. Minimum of 2 years experience post NATABOC certification. Salary Commensurate with experience and qualifications Minimum Qualifications Masters Degree Required. NATABOC Certification Required. Eligible for State of Mississippi Athletic Training Licensure/current holder of stated license. CPR /First Aid/ AED certification. Minimum of 2 years experience post NATABOC certification. Preferred Qualifications Special Instructions to Applicants Requires a high periods of concentration intermittently and normal attention. Lifting of equipment and injured student-athletes is required. Will require work outside in hot environments. Additional Information Posting Detail Information Open Date 03/27/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? DSU Employee DSU Job Website Invited by Department to Apply MS State Employment Service HigherEdJobs Chronicle of Higher Education Diverse Issues Indeed.com Other Will you now or in the future require \"sponsorship\" for an employment based visa status? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter/Letter of Application Optional Documents Other Document Delta State University is an Equal Employment Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer. Delta State University is committed to maintaining a learning and working environment free from sexual and gender-based discrimination or harassment. Our goal is for all to have equal access to the many great services and opportunities we offer. For more information, or to report an incident, see https://www.deltastate.edu/titleix/ or email titleix@deltastate.edu . To ensure the secur