chool counseling program. Primary responsibilities include but are not limited to: teaching courses in CACREP core and counseling specialty areas; providing clinical supervision to students; producing a focused line of research leading to publications in refereed journals and to external funding; advising/mentoring students; working with faculty in the Counselor Education program and with those entities affiliated with the program; recruiting for the program; participating actively in professional organizations and university committees, and continuously improving the program. Qualifications Doctorate in Counselor Education; emphasis and work experience in clinical mental health or school counseling preferred; graduate of CACREP accredited program; NCC certification; eligible for licensure as a Professional Counselor and Board Qualified Supervisor in Mississippi or your state of residence; evidence of clinical competence, successful teaching experience, and potential for excellence in scholarly achievement (e.g., research, publications, and presentations); demonstrated potential for leadership in school or clinical mental health counseling. Salary Commensurate with experience and qualifications Minimum Qualifications - Preferred Qualifications Special Instructions to Applicants Please list contact information for at least three references. Links to upload letters of reference will not be sent to the recommenders at this time. If you have letters of recommendation which you would like to submit at this time please upload them with your application under optional documents. You may also email them to DSUHRJobs@deltastate.edu and we will add them to your application materials. Additional Information Posting Detail Information Open Date 04/22/2025 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? DSU Employee DSU Job Website Invited by Department to Apply 