    "https://deltastate.peopleadmin.com/postings/4522": {
      "title": "Groundskeeper III",
      "description": "Delta State University Applicant Portal | Groundskeeper III Skip to Main Content About Academics admissions Student Life Athletics Alumni & Friends my DSU Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Groundskeeper III Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Groundskeeper III Working Title Groundskeeper III Position Type Staff Department Facilities Management Posting Number 201201427 Full or Part Time Full Time Benefit Eligible Yes If Other, Please Explain: Tenure/Non-Tenure Track Non-Tenure Track Salary Basis Hourly If Other, Please Explain: Position Summary Information Responsibilities The incumbent operates various power equipment used in the maintenance of campus grounds, gardens, sports fields, golf course, and to assure the upkeep of the University. Assist with training and oversight of other crew members in the completion of assigned maintenance duties. Picks up trash and debris from University grounds, parking areas, walks, streets, sports fields, ditches, culverts, and catch basins. Collects and removes debris and trash from campus and disposes of such through approved methods. Cuts lawns, trims and edges around walks, curbs, planting beds, and walls using appropriate grounds maintenance tools. Plants new landscape areas and renovates existing areas according to pre-approved plans. Waters lawns and plant materials, applies fertilizers. Sprays herbicides and pesticides mechanical and power sprayers. Rakes and removes leaves; cleans drainage ditches, culverts, and catch basins. Cleans building exteriors, entrances, and campus pavement areas using brooms, sweepers, power washers, and blowers/vacuums. Sweeps and cleans streets; removes snow, ice, and debris from streets and walks as required. Prunes shrubs, ground cover, ornamental grasses, and trees. Assists the Grounds Supervisor with modification and repair of irrigation PVC pipe and sprinkler heads. Patches holes in asphalt parking and driveways. Marks sports fields, paints parking striping and crosswalks. Maintains the grounds, athletic fields, and golf course in acceptable manner according to DSU and industry standards. Qualifications Ability to read, write, speak, and execute written and oral instructions. Ability to effectively maintain the University grounds and landscape with minimal oversight. Ability to operate maintenance and construction equipment including various types of tractors, skid loader, commercial mowers including zero-turn mowers, reel mowers, aerial lifts, line trimmers, edgers, blowers, tillers, street sweeper, roller/packer, verticutter, power washers, pesticide sprayers including power spraying equipment with booms, pruning equipment including chain saws and power pruners, paint striping machine, plate compactor, as well as typical maintenance hand tools. Ability to operate fertilizer spreader and golf/utility carts. Ability to back lap and adjust reel mowers. Ability to safety operate trucks and vans with trailers in tow and navigate safely through campus streets and narrow driveways. Must be able to lift a minimum of 80 pounds, climb ladders, work in tight spaces including trenches, and work outdoors in temperature and weather extremes. Salary Commensurate with experience and qualifications Minimum Qualifications Must be able to read, write, speak and understand oral and written instructions. Must have a High School degree or GED . Must have a valid US driver’s license and be insurable under DSU insurance carrier. Preferred Qualifications A minimum of 18 months of directly related grounds maintenance experience is preferred. Special Instructions to Applicants Additional Information Posting Detail Information Open Date 07/27/2023 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? DSU Employee DSU Job Website Invited by Department to Apply MS State Employment Service HigherEdJobs Chronicle of Higher Education Diverse Issues Indeed.com Other Do you have a high school degree or GED? yes no * Do you have a valid, current driver's license? yes no * How much experience do you have with lawn maintenance? less than six months less than one year more than one year * Will you now or in the future require \"sponsorship\" for an employment based visa status? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Resume Delta State University is an Equal Employment Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer. Delta State University is committed to maintaining a learning and working environment free from sexual and gender-based discrimination or harassment. Our goal is for all to have equal access to the many great services and opportunities we offer. For more information, or to report an incident, see https://www.deltastate.edu/titleix/ or email titleix@deltastate.edu . To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
