    "https://deltastate.peopleadmin.com/postings/5159": {
      "title": "McNair Scholars Program Coordinator",
      "description": "Delta State University Applicant Portal | McNair Scholars Program Coordinator Skip to Main Content About Academics admissions Student Life Athletics Alumni & Friends my DSU Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help McNair Scholars Program Coordinator Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title McNair Scholars Program Coordinator Working Title McNair Scholars Program Director Position Type Staff Department Grants and Contracts Posting Number 201201736 Full or Part Time Full Time Benefit Eligible Yes If Other, Please Explain: Tenure/Non-Tenure Track Salary Basis 12 month If Other, Please Explain: Position Summary Information Responsibilities Under the direction of the Executive Director of Sponsored Programs and Special Projects and the McNair Research Scholars Project Director, the McNair Research Scholars Coordinator will be responsible for the day-to-day management of the relationship between the program and the scholars, including data entry, travel with students, and maintaining up-to-date files on the students. Qualifications Bachelor’s degree or documented relevant experience or training; a minimum of five years of office work experience; excellent ability to utilize Microsoft Office and similar computer programs; experience working with students with backgrounds and experiences similar to McNair Research Scholars; experience with inputting and managing data; and excellent communication skills. Salary Commensurate with experience, qualifications, and university’s resources. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree or documented relevant experience or training; a minimum of five years of office work experience; excellent ability to utilize Microsoft Office and similar computer programs; experience working with students with backgrounds and experiences similar to McNair Research Scholars; experience with inputting and managing data; and excellent communication skills. Preferred Qualifications Preference will be given to qualified candidates with university work experience; experience managing organization newsletters, calendars, and social media; and experience working in TRIO programs or federal grant programs. Special Instructions to Applicants Additional Information Posting Detail Information Open Date 07/01/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? DSU Employee DSU Job Website Invited by Department to Apply MS State Employment Service HigherEdJobs Chronicle of Higher Education Diverse Issues Indeed.com Other * Will you now or in the future require \"sponsorship\" for an employment based visa status? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Unofficial Transcripts Optional Documents Other Document Letter of Reference 1 Letter of Reference 2 Letter of Reference 3 Delta State University is an Equal Employment Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer. Delta State University is committed to maintaining a learning and working environment free from sexual and gender-based discrimination or harassment. Our goal is for all to have equal access to the many great services and opportunities we offer. For more information, or to report an incident, see https://www.deltastate.edu/titleix/ or email titleix@deltastate.edu . To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
