    "https://deltastate.peopleadmin.com/postings/5182": {
      "title": "Academic Advisor",
      "description": "Delta State University Applicant Portal | Academic Advisor - 2 positions available Skip to Main Content About Academics admissions Student Life Athletics Alumni & Friends my DSU Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Academic Advisor - 2 positions available Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please include the names and contact information of 3-5 references. Letters of recommendation are optional. If you would like to add a letter of recommendation, please upload them with your application under optional documents. You may also have them emailed to DSUHRJobs@deltastate.edu. Once letters are received we will add them to your application materials. Posting Details Position Information Job Title Academic Advisor - 2 positions available Working Title Academic Advisor Position Type Staff Department Academic Advising Posting Number 201201730 Full or Part Time Full Time Benefit Eligible Yes If Other, Please Explain: Tenure/Non-Tenure Track Non-Tenure Track Salary Basis 12 month If Other, Please Explain: Position Summary Information Responsibilities Provide comprehensive academic advisement and support to assigned students within a designated college at Delta State University. Assist students with appropriate course selection and understanding academic program requirements. Identify resources to assist students with success in their chosen program of study. Work collaboratively with faculty, staff, other advisors and campus personnel to facilitate fully coordinated services for incoming students. Teach a 3-hour First Year Seminar class each semester. Develop and implement registration activities. Review transcripts for students changing majors or transferring. Provide ongoing communication and support to both new and returning advisees to ensure their academic and personal success. Provide data and reports on academic advising and student success indicators. Other related duties as assigned. Qualifications A minimum of a bachelor’s degree in education, counseling, psychology, student affairs, or a related field is typically required. A master’s degree in a relevant field is preferred. Candidates should have experience working with students, providing support, guidance, and information about academic programs and university policies. Experience in identifying student needs, conducting early interventions, and connecting students with appropriate resources and support systems. Thorough understanding of academic programs, degree requirements, and university policies and procedures. Strong communication skills, both verbal and written, and excellent interpersonal skills. Additionally, strong organizational skills, attention to detail, and the ability to manage multiple tasks and priorities. Salary Commensurate with experience, qualifications, and university’s resources. Minimum Qualifications A minimum of a bachelor’s degree in education, counseling, psychology, student affairs, or a related field is typically required. Candidates should have experience working with students, providing support, guidance, and information about academic programs and university policies. Experience in identifying student needs, conducting early interventions, and connecting students with appropriate resources and support systems. Thorough understanding of academic programs, degree requirements, and university policies and procedures. Strong communication skills, both verbal and written, and excellent interpersonal skills. Additionally, strong organizational skills, attention to detail, and the ability to manage multiple tasks and priorities. Preferred Qualifications A master’s degree in a relevant field is preferred. Experience in academic advising, student success, enrollment management, or higher education administration is preferred, along with strong interpersonal, communication, and organizational skills and the ability to work effectively with diverse student populations. Special Instructions to Applicants Please include the names and contact information of 3-5 references. Letters of recommendation are optional. If you would like to add a letter of recommendation, please upload them with your application under optional documents. You may also have them emailed to DSUHRJobs@deltastate.edu. Once letters are received we will add them to your application materials. Additional Information Posting Detail Information Open Date 06/22/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? DSU Employee DSU Job Website Invited by Department to Apply MS State Employment Service HigherEdJobs Chronicle of Higher Education Diverse Issues Indeed.com Other * Will you now or in the future require \"sponsorship\" for an employment based visa status? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter/Letter of Application Unofficial Transcripts Optional Documents Other Document Letter of Reference 1 Letter of Reference 2 Letter of Reference 3 Delta State University is an Equal Employment Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer. Delta State University is committed to maintaining a learning and working environment free from sexual and gender-based discrimination or harassment. Our goal is for all to have equal access to the many great services and opportunities we offer. For more information, or to report an incident, see https://www.deltastate.edu/titleix/ or email titleix@deltastate.edu . 