    "https://deltastate.peopleadmin.com/postings/5171": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in Marketing",
      "description": "Delta State University Applicant Portal | Assistant Professor in Marketing Skip to Main Content About Academics admissions Student Life Athletics Alumni & Friends my DSU Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Professor in Marketing Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Assistant Professor in Marketing Working Title Assistant Professor in Marketing Position Type Faculty Department Mgmt., Marketing and Business Administration Posting Number 201201721 Full or Part Time Full Time Benefit Eligible Yes If Other, Please Explain: Tenure/Non-Tenure Track Tenure Track Salary Basis 9 month If Other, Please Explain: Position Summary Information Responsibilities The primary responsibilities of this position are to teach undergraduate and graduate courses in Marketing and related fields. A typical course load is 12 credit hours per semester. Other expected responsibilities include: Advising students Mentoring and guiding students in the field Participating in curriculum review, development, and assessment Recruiting for the healthcare administration program Providing department, college, university, community, and professional service Participating in scholarly research Participating in professional organizations Candidates must be willing to teach online, hi-flex/hybrid, and traditional classroom courses, as well as team-teach with other professors. Qualifications PhD or DBA in Marketing or a closely related field. ABD candidates in the final stages of dissertation will be considered. Candidates must have a potential or demonstrated commitment to scholarly research. Candidates must be authorized to work in the United States. Salary Commensurate with experience and qualifications Minimum Qualifications PhD or DBA in Marketing or a closely related field. ABD candidates in the final stages of dissertation will be considered. Evidence of or potential for scholarly activity. Candidate must be authorized to work in the United States. Preferred Qualifications PhD in Marketing or closely related field from an AACSB or ACBSP -accredited school. ABD candidates in final stages of dissertation will be considered. Track record of scholarly activity and relevant industry experience. Special Instructions to Applicants Additional Information Start date for this position is Spring 2027 (January 2027) Posting Detail Information Open Date 05/21/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? DSU Employee DSU Job Website Invited by Department to Apply MS State Employment Service HigherEdJobs Chronicle of Higher Education Diverse Issues Indeed.com Other * Will you now or in the future require \"sponsorship\" for an employment based visa status? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter/Letter of Application Unofficial Transcripts Teaching Philosophy Optional Documents Resume Other Document Letter of Reference 1 Letter of Reference 2 Letter of Reference 3 Delta State University is an Equal Employment Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer. Delta State University is committed to maintaining a learning and working environment free from sexual and gender-based discrimination or harassment. Our goal is for all to have equal access to the many great services and opportunities we offer. For more information, or to report an incident, see https://www.deltastate.edu/titleix/ or email titleix@deltastate.edu . To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
