    "https://deltastate.peopleadmin.com/postings/5074": {
      "title": "Flight Instructor (Multiple Positions)",
      "description": "Delta State University Applicant Portal | Flight Instructor (Multiple Positions) Skip to Main Content About Academics admissions Student Life Athletics Alumni & Friends my DSU Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Flight Instructor (Multiple Positions) Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please submit copies of: FAA Flight Certificates (front and back) FAA Medical Three letters of recommendation are required. Requests for letters of recommendation will automatically be generated to the references you list on the application. They will be sent a link to allow them to submit letter directly to application. It is the applicant’s responsibility to follow up with the references to ensure the letters have been submitted. Posting Details Position Information Job Title Flight Instructor (Multiple Positions) Working Title Flight Instructor (Multiple Positions) Position Type Staff Department Commercial Aviation Posting Number 201200957 Full or Part Time Part Time Benefit Eligible No If Other, Please Explain: Tenure/Non-Tenure Track Non-Tenure Track Salary Basis Hourly If Other, Please Explain: Position Summary Information Responsibilities Delta State flight courses include: Primary single engine, Instrument Airplane, Multi-Engine Instrument add-on to Private Certificate, Initial Commercial Multi-Engine, Single-Engine add-on to Commercial Certificate, Initial Multi-Engine Flight Instructor, Single-Engine Add-on to CFI , and Instrument Flight Instructor. The Flight Instructor is responsible for providing student training in accordance with Delta State University’s Commercial Aviation Department’s FAA Part 141 Policies: FOM , Appropriate TCO , and Flight Instructor Manual. Qualifications Must have a Current FAA Certified Flight Instructor, Single Engine Certificate. Must have a Current Second Class FAA Medical Prefer in addition to CFI Single engine: Instrument Flight Instructor and Multi Engine Flight Instructor Salary Commensurate with experience, qualifications, and university’s resources. Minimum Qualifications Must have a Current FAA Certified Flight Instructor Certificate Must have a Current Second Class FAA Medical Preferred Qualifications Prefer a Current FAA Certified Flight Instructor, Single Engine Certificate, Multi Engine Certificate, Instrument Instructor Certificate. Must have a Current Second Class FAA Medical Prefer in addition to CFI Single engine: Instrument Flight Instructor and Multi Engine Flight Instructor Special Instructions to Applicants Please submit copies of: FAA Flight Certificates (front and back) FAA Medical Three letters of recommendation are required. Requests for letters of recommendation will automatically be generated to the references you list on the application. They will be sent a link to allow them to submit letter directly to application. It is the applicant’s responsibility to follow up with the references to ensure the letters have been submitted. Additional Information This position is advertised continuously because of multiple hires made throughout the year. Posting Detail Information Open Date 10/04/2019 Close Date Open Until Filled No Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? DSU Employee DSU Job Website Invited by Department to Apply MS State Employment Service HigherEdJobs Chronicle of Higher Education Diverse Issues Indeed.com Other * Will you now or in the future require \"sponsorshi