    "https://deltastate.peopleadmin.com/postings/5142": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Leadership and Research",
      "description": "Delta State University Applicant Portal | Assistant Professor of Leadership and Research Skip to Main Content About Academics admissions Student Life Athletics Alumni & Friends my DSU Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Professor of Leadership and Research Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Assistant Professor of Leadership and Research Working Title Assistant Professor of Leadership and Research Position Type Faculty Department School of Leadership, Research, & Psychology Posting Number 201201725 Full or Part Time Full Time Benefit Eligible Yes If Other, Please Explain: Tenure/Non-Tenure Track Tenure Track Salary Basis 9 month If Other, Please Explain: Position Summary Information Responsibilities The primary responsibilities of the person assuming this position will be teaching graduate classes in leadership and/or research, mentoring students, conducting research, publishing in professional journals, serving on various committees, and assuming responsibility for helping to develop and maintain quality curriculum and instruction and doctoral programs in the School of Leadership, Research, and Psychology. An additional role will be serving as the Department Chair. Additionally, the successful candidate will also be expected to serve on doctoral committees, support the assignment of dissertation committees, and perform other duties as assigned by the Dean of the CEAH and the Chair of the School of Leadership, Research, and Psychology. Qualifications The candidate must have an earned doctoral degree in Leadership and/or Research or other research-related field. Area of specialization should complement leadership for Higher Education settings. Teaching experience at the post-secondary level and evidence of research productivity are required. Preference will be given to candidates who have experience teaching leadership courses, research methods, and educational research writing courses. Evidence of supporting students through the dissertation process is also essential. Salary Commensurate with experience, qualifications, and university’s resources. Minimum Qualifications Candidates with a Doctorate in Leadership, Research, or other research-related field. Teaching experience at the post-secondary level and evidence of research productivity are required. Preferred Qualifications An earned doctoral degree in Leadership, Research, or other research-related field. Area of specialization should complement leadership for Higher Education settings. Teaching experience at the post-secondary level and evidence of research productivity are required. Preference will be given to candidates who have experience teaching leadership courses, research methods, and educational research writing courses. Evidence of supporting students through the dissertation process is also essential. Special Instructions to Applicants Additional Information Posting Detail Information Open Date 06/15/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? DSU Employee DSU Job Website Invited by Department to Apply MS State Employment Service HigherEdJobs Chronicle of Higher Education Diverse Issues Indeed.com Other * Will you now or in the future require \"sponsorship\" for an employment based visa status? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter/Letter of Application Teaching Philosophy Unofficial Transcripts Optional Documents Other Document Letter of Reference 1 Letter of Reference 2 Letter of Reference 3 Delta State University is an Equal Employment Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer. Delta State University is committed to maintaining a learning and working environment free from sexual and gender-based discrimination or harassment. Our goal is for all to have equal access to the many great services and opportunities we offer. For more information, or to report an incident, see https://www.deltastate.edu/titleix/ or email titleix@deltastate.edu . To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://deltastate.peopleadmin.com/postings/5046": {
      "title": "Administrative Specialist",
      "description": "Delta State University Applicant Portal | Administrative Specialist Skip to Main Content About Academics admissions Student Life Athletics Alumni & Friends my DSU Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Administrative Specialist Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Administrative Specialist Working Title Administrative Specialist Position Type Staff Department Grants and Contracts Posting Number 201201690 Full or Part Time Full Time Benefit Eligible Yes If Other, Please Explain: Tenure/Non-Tenure Track Non-Tenure Track Salary Basis 12 month If Other, Please Explain: Position Summary Information Responsibilities Administrative Support: Serve as the primary point of contact for all departmental inquiries and correspondence. Maintain calendars, schedule meetings, and coordinate events and workshops across all three units. Prepare agendas, meeting minutes, memos, and official correspondence. Organize and maintain digital and physical filing systems for each department. Program Coordination: Support the planning and execution of academic development events, cultural programs, and grant-funded initiatives. Assist with logistics for internal and external programming, including room reservations, catering, technology setup, and travel arrangements. Track project timelines, deliverables, and reporting requirements. Fiscal and Grant Support: Process purchase requests, reimbursements, and budget tracking in accordance with university policies. Assist with grant budget monitoring, data collection, and financial reporting documentation. Coordinate invoicing and vendor communications related to programmatic needs. Communications and Outreach: Manage content updates for departmental websites and social media platforms. Draft newsletters, promotional materials, and stakeholder communications. Serve as liaison between departments and internal/external partners. Data and Records Management: Collect and organize data for departmental reports and grant applications. Maintain up-to-date databases of program participants, stakeholders, and funding records. Qualifications See Below Salary Commensurate with experience, qualifications, and university’s resources. Minimum Qualifications Required: Bachelor’s degree in business administration, education, communications, or a related field. Minimum of 2 years of administrative or project coordination experience. Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Strong organizational skills with the ability to manage multiple tasks and deadlines. Proficiency in Microsoft Word, and advanced experience in Excel Preferred Qualifications Preferred: Experience in higher education or non-profit administration. Familiarity with grant administration and compliance, especially complex budgets Knowledge of regional culture, education, and institutional development. Special Instructions to Applicants Additional Information Posting Detail Information Open Date 03/08/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled No Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? DSU Employee DSU Job Website Invited by Department to Apply MS State Employment Service HigherEdJobs Chronicle of Higher Education Diverse Issues Indeed.com Other * Will you now or in the future require \"sponsorship\" for an employment based visa status? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter/Letter of Application Writing Sample Unofficial Transcripts 