    "https://deltastate.peopleadmin.com/postings/4539": {
      "title": "Custodian",
      "description": "Delta State University Applicant Portal | Custodian Skip to Main Content About Academics admissions Student Life Athletics Alumni & Friends my DSU Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Custodian Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Start Date of Employment to be Determined. Posting Details Position Information Job Title Custodian Working Title Custodian Position Type Staff Department Custodial Services - Facilities Posting Number 201201478 Full or Part Time Full Time Benefit Eligible Yes If Other, Please Explain: Tenure/Non-Tenure Track Non-Tenure Track Salary Basis Hourly If Other, Please Explain: Position Summary Information Responsibilities Cleans and dusts areas such as suites, offices, classrooms, kitchens, living spaces, laboratories, lobbies, museums, locker rooms, stairways, corridors and elevators. Make beds as required. Dust, mops and wet mops floors. Cleans and polishes furniture and cleans inside windows on floor level. Cleans and maintains restrooms and bathrooms. Clean glass, chalkboards, display cases, interior partitions and light fixtures which are reachable from the floor. Refill toilet paper, paper towel and soap dispensers. Clean and polish hardware such as doors, woodwork, door handles, push plates, kick plates, metal handrails and drinking fountains. Vacuums and spot clean rugs. Removes and cleans floor mats and entrance rug runners. Maintains custodial and storage areas in a clean orderly manner. Maintain adequate supply of cleaning equipment, materials and supplies. Use cleaning tools such as mops, brooms, squeegees, cleaning cloths, sponges, pails, brushes, vacuum cleaners, etc. Turn in found articles in accordance with University policy. Remove waste paper baskets and containers, and empties same into trash containers and cleans area after trash has been picked up. Remove snow, ice and littler from building entrances or sweep same. Reports all repairs required and safety and fire hazards to building secretary and immediate supervisor. Observe safety standards and practices. Lift and carry objects of at least 30-60 pounds unassisted. Perform related duties as required or assigned within job classification. Qualifications Minimum of one year in cleaning services or related type work. Ability to read, write and follow written instructions. Must have a valid, US drivers license. Salary Commensurate with experience and qualifications Minimum Qualifications Minimum of 6 months in cleaning services or related type work. Ability to read, write and follow written instructions. Must have a valid, US drivers license. Preferred Qualifications Minimum of one year in cleaning services or related type work. Ability to read, write and follow written instructions. Special Instructions to Applicants Start Date of Employment to be Determined. Additional Information Posting Detail Information Open Date 04/01/2024 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? DSU Employee DSU Job Website Invited by Department to Apply MS State Employment Service HigherEdJobs Chronicle of Higher Education Diverse Issues Indeed.com Other * Do you have a valid, current US driver's license? Yes No * Are you a U.S. citizen or have lawful authorization to work in the U.S.? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Delta State University is an Equal Employment Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer. Delta State University is committed to maintaining a learning and working environment free from sexual and gender-based discrimination or harassment. Our goal is for all to have equal access to the many great services and opportunities we offer. For more information, or to report an incident, see https://www.deltastate.edu/titleix/ or email titleix@deltastate.edu . To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://deltastate.peopleadmin.com/postings/5181": {
      "title": "International Admissions Specialist, International Student Services",
      "description": "Delta State University Applicant Portal | International Admissions Specialist, International Student Services Skip to Main Content About Academics admissions Student Life Athletics Alumni & Friends my DSU Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help International Admissions Specialist, International Student Services Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title International Admissions Specialist, International Student Services Working Title International Admissions Specialist, International Student Services Position Type Staff Department Student Success Center Posting Number 201201743 Full or Part Time Full Time Benefit Eligible Yes If Other, Please Explain: Tenure/Non-Tenure Track Non-Tenure Track Salary Basis 12 month If Other, Please Explain: Position Summary Information Responsibilities International Student Services is a division of the DSU Student Success Center. The International Admissions Specialist is a full-time, 12-month position that reports to the Coordinator of International Student Services. This position works closely with the International Assistant Advisor, campus constituencies, and other team members in the Student Success Center. Responsibilities: Assist international applicants, update applicant checklists, correspond with applicants regarding necessary document corrections; Review, code, and enter undergraduate and graduate admissions’ documents into Banner; Assist applicants who require admissions’ deferral due to personal or visa reasons; Maintain International admissions’ email to ensure up-to-date, accurate information; Communicate regularly with active applicants and monitor inactive applications; Monitor international student records to ensure compliance with SEVIS / USCIS /F1 visa requirements and guidelines, including progress towards degree and required full-time enrollment status; Serve as a Designated School Official ( DSO ) in SEVIS to create student accounts, issue, and maintain student I-20’s, register students at beginning of each academic term, update employment, etc.; Maintain international student insurance policies by working closely with students, insurance provider and DSU Student Business Services to ensure timely insurance processing; Collaborate with team members to plan and implement strategies to increase international recruiting opportunities and to improve current international student retention and development; Supervise DSU student employees, including work-study, RSE , and graduate assistants; Coordinate special events, new student orientation, and current student check-in/check-out before/after holidays and breaks; Assist with on/off-campus employment/internship review and approval processing; Serve as Campus Coordinator for exchange programs through coordination with IREX and international exchange students; Follow guidelines with Family Educational Rights and Privacy Act of 1974 ( FERPA ) as they pertain to the students’ rights to privacy and accuracy and retention of academic records; and, Perform other duties as assigned as related to international admissions and retention. Qualifications Bachelor’s degree required; 1-3 years of experience in higher education admissions preferred; Proficient in Word, PowerPoint, Excel, social media required; with Banner experience preferred; Demonstrated record of: Strong leadership, interpersonal and oral/written communication skills with ability to prioritize multiple tasks in a changing, evolving department/Integrity and commitment to developing and maintaining the highest academic standards and working with a diverse population of students, faculty, and staff/Plan and budget time wisely, be motivated and take initiative/Must be a United States citizen or have legal authorization to work in the United States. Salary Commensurate with experience, qualifications, and university’s resources. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree; Proficient in Word, PowerPoint, Excel, social media; Demonstrated record of: Strong leadership, interpersonal and oral/written communication skills with ability to prioritize multiple tasks in a changing, evolving department/Integrity and commitment to developing and maintaining the highest academic standards and working with a diverse population of students, faculty, and staff/Plan and budget time wisely, be motivated and take initiative/Must be a United States citizen or have legal authorization to work in the United States. Preferred Qualifications 1-3 years of experience in higher education admissions; Banner experience Special Instructions to Applicants Additional Information Posting Detail Information Open Date 08/21/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? DSU Employee DSU Job Website Invited by Department to Apply MS State Employment Service HigherEdJobs Chronicle of Higher Education Diverse Issues Indeed.com Other * Will you now or in the future require \"sponsorship\" for an employment based visa status? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter/Letter of Application Unofficial Transcripts Optional Documents Letter of Reference 1 Letter of Reference 2 Letter of Reference 3 Other Document Delta State University is an Equal Employment Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer. Delta State University is committed to maintaining a learning and working environment free from sexual and gender-based discrimination or harassment. Our goal is for all to have equal access to the many great services and opportunities we offer. For more information, or to report an incident, see https://www.deltastate.edu/titleix/ or email titleix@deltastate.edu . To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
